On Tue, Dec 5, 2017 at 12:56 AM, Gabriel Ferreira <gsferr...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi Nick,
>
> I am running an analysis with a fossil-only tree, of a Devonian-Silurian clade and when I try to divide up the tree into 5 periods with my timeperiods file BioGeoBEARS returns the following error message:
>
> Error in scan(file = file, what = "", sep = "\n", quiet = TRUE, skip = skip, : 'file' must be a character string or connection
>
> I tried using a timeperiods table with the real ages (i.e., varying from 377.4 to 430.5) and with ages scaled to 0 (i.e., varying from 0.1 - 53.1) but on both cases, I get the same message. I also tried to use only two periods (to avoid potential few taxa problems), but it happens the same
>

Hi -- this error is about something else, it indicates that some file is not being found.

E.g. you would probably get it if you had:

BioGeoBEARS_run_object$timesfn = timeperiods.txt

...instead of:

BioGeoBEARS_run_object$timesfn = "timeperiods.txt"

...or if the file was misnamed, not in your working directory, etc.

Re: time scaling, BioGeoBEARS (and any other program) will treat the highest tip in the tree as time 0, whatever the absolute time, so yes, you should scale the times accordingly.

Cheers!
Nick

> Hope you can help me.
> Thanks in advance.
> Best wishes,
